//? Title: Inference Buffers: Fixed Storage and Repeated Calls
//? Subtitle: Stable public buffers do not imply allocation-free internal execution
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A caller integrating a predictor into a native loop needs known input/output sizes and stable
buffer ownership. We repeatedly fill one input tensor and copy predictions into one output
tensor, including a return to the first input. This eager CPU example illustrates buffer
contracts; it does not parse or execute a TFLite FlatBuffer.
)
\toc

> The method

For one row with two Float32 inputs and one output, the public buffers contain 8 and 4 bytes.
The consumer keeps their tensor handles alive and replaces contents in place. The same affine
weights are reused for every call:

$$
\mathrm{output}_{1\times1}\leftarrow\mathrm{input}_{1\times2}W_{2\times1}+b_1.
$$
\alttext(The output buffer receives the two-feature affine computation without replacing its storage.)

A NoGradGuard prevents graph recording. affine_inference returns a temporary tensor, which is
copied into the persistent output buffer; matrix multiplication may allocate temporaries. Thus
stable public addresses do not establish allocation-free inference, compilation, quantization,
delegate acceleration or TFLite compatibility. Model initialization and input validation occur
before the repeated calls; each call costs O(input_width times output_width) in this fixture.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/tflite_inference_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/tflite_inference_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/tflite_inference_concept.tikz > build/tflite_inference_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/tflite_inference_concept.svg build/tflite_inference_concept.dvi > build/tflite_inference_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/tflite_inference_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
// result_begin:
