\alttext(Persistent input; 2 Float32 = 8 bytes Then Native affine function; temporary result Then Persistent output; 1 Float32 = 4 bytes.)

> Simple examples

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tflite_inference_reuse.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;auto input=n::zeros({1,2}),output=n::zeros({1,1});
 const auto w=n::tensor({.75,-1.5},{2,1}),b=n::tensor({.25});
 const auto* in_address=input.data_ptr<float>();const auto* out_address=output.data_ptr<float>();
 const std::vector<std::vector<double>> queries{{0,0},{1,0},{0,1},{2,-3},{0,0}};
 std::vector<double> actual,expected,index;
 for(size_t i=0;i<queries.size();++i){n::NoGradGuard guard;input.copy_(n::from_vector(queries[i],{1,2}));output.copy_(n::affine_inference(input,w,b));
 actual.push_back(output.item());expected.push_back(.75*queries[i][0]-1.5*queries[i][1]+.25);index.push_back(i);
 if(input.data_ptr<float>()!=in_address||output.data_ptr<float>()!=out_address||actual.back()!=expected.back())return 1;}
 auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.lines(index,actual,"reused output buffer")
 .title("The first input gives the same result after reuse").x_label("call index").y_label("prediction");
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");p.size(820,420).save_svg("build/tflite_inference_reuse.svg");
 dm::dstruct::DataFrame t;t.add_column("call",index);t.add_column("expected",expected);t.add_column("actual",actual);std::print("{}\n\nPublic buffers: {} input bytes, {} output bytes; addresses unchanged.\n",t.to_md(),input.numel()*sizeof(float),output.numel()*sizeof(float));
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| call | expected | actual |
| ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 0 | 0.25 | 0.25 |
| 1 | 1.00 | 1.00 |
| 2 | -1.25 | -1.25 |
| 3 | 6.25 | 6.25 |
| 4 | 0.25 | 0.25 |


Public buffers: 8 input bytes, 4 output bytes; addresses unchanged.
\image(figures/tflite_inference_reuse.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Repeated inputs produce repeated outputs with stable input and output storage.)
\alttext(Repeated inputs produce repeated outputs with stable input and output storage.)

> Checking the theory

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;int bad=0;const auto w=n::tensor({.75,-1.5},{2,1});
 try{n::affine_inference(n::zeros({1,2}),w,n::zeros({2}));}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++bad;}
 try{n::decode_npz(std::vector<unsigned char>(16,0));}catch(const std::exception&){++bad;}
 if(bad!=2)return 1;std::print("Bad bias shape and invalid model archive rejected: {}.\n",bad);
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Bad bias shape and invalid model archive rejected: 2.
// result_end


> Conclusion

The public input and output addresses remain stable across five calls, and returning to the first
input reproduces its output. The internal eager operation still allocates a result. For real TFLite
files, a TFLite interpreter and its own allocation/signature API are required.

